# adf-ledger byte-freeze — git must NEVER rewrite line endings on hashed artifacts.
#
# Every sealed claim set, resolution, and pulse in this repo is a HASHED artifact:
# its recorded SHA-256 (the .sha256 sidecar) and its OpenTimestamps proof (.ots)
# attest the EXACT bytes. If git flipped LF<->CRLF on checkout, a visitor on a
# different OS would recompute a different hash and the proof would look broken.
# These rules keep verification durable across every clone and platform.
#
#   -text  = never normalize line endings (store + check out bytes verbatim)
#   binary = -text -diff (opaque bytes; no diffing, no normalization)

sealed/**       -text
resolutions/**  -text
pulses/**       -text
*.sha256        -text
*.ots           binary
